1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,625
Flutter web attribute setters can report success before the underlying update

2
00:00:04,625 --> 00:00:08,950
finishes. When that update fails, the caller never receives the error.

3
00:00:09,767 --> 00:00:14,795
The app first configures the real Test Store, then the browser goes offline.

4
00:00:14,795 --> 00:00:19,050
All four setter futures report success, while their JavaScript promises reject

5
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:19,437
separately.

6
00:00:20,237 --> 00:00:25,111
The shared setters return promises. The Dart web handlers discard them, so

7
00:00:25,111 --> 00:00:28,767
their futures complete immediately and lose the asynchronous failures.

8
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:32,617
The fix awaits and converts each JavaScript promise.

9
00:00:32,617 --> 00:00:36,807
The returned future now represents the actual operation and propagates its

10
00:00:36,807 --> 00:00:38,330
rejection to the caller.

11
00:00:39,137 --> 00:00:43,912
In the same offline scenario, all four calls now report caught errors with

12
00:00:43,912 --> 00:00:47,218
no unhandled rejections. All twelve focused Chrome checks pass.

13
00:00:47,218 --> 00:00:50,157
This defect is specific to the web implementation.
